      "text": "<b>Your year 10 goals</b>\nEconomic 75 · Social 75 · Environmental 60\nEvery run gets an ending.\n\nIn this fictional Meadowbrook community, four households share a farm store, a small village square and a recreation ground. Productive fields sit between woodland and creek corridors. Add homes and livelihoods while keeping those corridors intact.\n\n32 open plots · 60 m grid; large projects use joined cells. Seven existing community plots remain in place. Woodland, water and protected areas cannot be built over.\n\nYou have $10M in public funds and ten years. The community starts with 4 of 16 needed homes and 4 of 36 target jobs. Queue a plan, then End Year to pay and advance construction. Upkeep reserves future funds.\n\nFictional scenario · shared weather and economic reference: Coon Valley, Wisconsin; other parameters are authored. Previous-layout saves are retained separately.",
